to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-13 : List (List Word)
to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-13 = cons "- **The three decisions, around 1970.** (1) The file system made the unit of storage untyped bytes," (cons "  and everything above inherited meaninglessness. (2) The personal computer was an isolated box, then" (cons "  networked as client to server, so every machine became an endpoint of someone else's machine. (3)" (cons "  The graphical interface gave each program its own window and world, turning the separation of" (cons "  programs into the shape of the screen. Done right the first time: a thing on the machine is a term" (cons "  with its type and an identity by content; machines meet as peers exchanging terms and checking what" (cons "  they receive; the screen shows the person's own things through views the person owns and can" (cons "  change." nil)))))))
